# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# This repo is developed on Windows, where `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout. The images we build run Linux. A file with a shebang and
# CRLF endings that is COPYed into a container fails at runtime with an error
# that tells you nothing useful:
#
#     exec /app/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# The file is right there. The kernel is looking for an interpreter literally
# named "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist. This is the single most common
# Windows -> Docker failure, and it costs people hours the first time.
#
# `.gitattributes` overrides `core.autocrlf` per-repository, so the repo behaves
# identically on Windows, Linux, CI runners, and inside images — regardless of
# any individual developer's global git config.

# Default: normalize every text file to LF, in the repo AND the working copy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces on the files that actually break containers when wrong.
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.bash        text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.dockerfile  text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint* text eol=lf
entrypoint*   text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts genuinely want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never transform binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
